{# What this provider holds of the signed-in person, and what they may correct of it, edited in place
   (issue beffroi-auth/op#17). It overrides the page of the bundle by its name, which is what §5.2 provides
   for, and the controllers of this application answer its two routes: the bundle serves the same thing as
   bare HTML with a form token, and this is what it looks like written with symfony/form.

   Two panels, because the page answers two questions: the account this provider keeps, which nobody
   changes here, and what it holds of the person. One line per claim in that second one, read where it is
   held and written where the tenant opens it: the same claim is not read in one list and offered in
   another, so somebody corrects what they are reading. What they have changed of it is a page of its own
   (beffroi-auth/beffroi#482), and the way there is what this page offers.

   Edited in place, and with no script: the value a person reads is the field they type into, and the
   button that saves it appears when the line is touched. That is a stylesheet (assets/styles/app.css) and
   not a behaviour, so a browser that runs nothing still shows a field and a button that work. #}
{% extends '@Beffroi/layout.html.twig' %}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}

{% block title %}{{ 'profile.title'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{% block action %}
    <a href="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account_profile_changes') }}" data-profile="changes">{{ 'changes.title'|trans }}</a>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    {{ include('@Beffroi/account/back.html.twig') }}
    <p>{{ 'profile.explanation'|trans }}</p>

    <section data-panel="account">
        <h2>{{ 'profile.account'|trans }}</h2>
        <dl data-information="account">
            {% for detail in identity %}
                {{ include('@Beffroi/account/detail.html.twig', {detail: detail}) }}
            {% endfor %}
        </dl>
    </section>

    <section data-panel="claims">
        <h2>{{ 'profile.about_you'|trans }}</h2>
        {% if held == 0 %}<p data-claims="none">{{ 'profile.none'|trans }}</p>{% endif %}
        {% if forms is empty %}
            <p data-changeable="none">{{ 'profile.change_nothing'|trans }}</p>
        {% else %}
            <p>{{ 'profile.change_explanation'|trans }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        <ul data-information="claims" data-claims="{{ held }}">
            {% for detail in claims %}
                {% set form = forms[detail.key] ?? null %}
                {% if form is not null %}
                    {# the field this form was built for, carried by the view (App\Form\ClaimType): what the
                       suggestions of a set of several hundred are drawn from, and what says there are any #}
                    {% set field = form.vars.field %}
                    <li data-claim="{{ detail.key }}">
                        {{ form_start(form, {attr: {'data-editable': detail.key}}) }}
                            {{ form_label(form.value) }}
                            {{ form_widget(form.value) }}
                            {# A set of several hundred is typed into with the whole set suggested
                               (beffroi-auth/beffroi#479). No type of the component renders a datalist and
                               these pages run no script, so the page renders it beside the field and the
                               field names it. #}
                            {% if field.isPicked %}
                                <datalist id="claim-{{ detail.key }}-values" data-values="{{ field.choices|length }}">
                                    {% for value, label in field.choices %}
                                        <option value="{{ value }}">{{ label }}</option>
                                    {% endfor %}
                                </datalist>
                            {% endif %}
                            <button type="submit" data-save>{{ 'profile.save'|trans }}</button>
                            {{ form_errors(form.value) }}
                            {{ form_help(form.value) }}
                        {{ form_end(form) }}
                    </li>
                {% elseif detail.value is not null or detail.moment is not null %}
                    {{ include('@Beffroi/account/claim.html.twig', {detail: detail}) }}
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
